Subject: [PATCH] hid: nanosic: derive folio posture and release covered inputs

Combine the existing connector reports with the active-low GPIO23 folded
hall. Observe GPIO10 through gpio-keys without claiming it twice. Release
HID keys, buttons and contacts before suppressing folded/covered input,
and resample posture before delivering pending input after resume.

GPIO23 polarity and the need for host-side gating were measured by
Seeker0472/liuqin-nixos at 73e8071e09880aeb47f0a427b9a65b8cc10927c4;
see docs/PORTING-NOTES.md and pkgs/kernel/patches/0002-liuqin-input-hid-touchscreen.patch.
This adaptation retains the local event-driven connection detection.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/nanosic,wn8030.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/nanosic,wn8030.yaml
index 04c023193..50fff3b07 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/nanosic,wn8030.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/nanosic,wn8030.yaml
@@ -54,6 +54,13 @@ properties:
   vdd-supply:
     description: Supply feeding the connector's pogo pins.
 
+  tablet-mode-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: >
+      Optional hall switch asserted when the folio is folded onto the back.
+      It does not detect a detached keyboard. The driver combines this state
+      with connector reports from the MCU and uses both GPIO edges as IRQs.
+
   wakeup-source: true
 
 required:
